     वर्ष/साल/माह/महीना/दिन/सप्ताह/व्यक्ति — "एक बार" parses to nothing. Writing
     "एक बार में एक वर्ष" made `numbers` FAIL (missing 1×2). Kept the digit and
     reworded to "गतिविधि स्थगन की अवधि 1 बार में 1 वर्ष से अधिक नहीं हो सकती";
     "1 माह" → "एक माह" was applied (parses fine).
  2. b#34 (016) "क्रम 1": "प्रथम क्रम" made `numbers` FAIL (missing 1×2) — there is
     no hi entry in ORDINAL_WORD_N. Kept "क्रम 1 में आते हैं".
  3. b#28 (012) "हेडलाइट 1 बार" and "वाहन संख्या 1 / 2": same lexicon gap
     (no "बार" unit, no Hindi ordinals). Digits kept; the other numeral calques in
     that file ("2 या अधिक वाहन", "हॉर्न 2 बार") were converted to words.
  4. b#49 (015) "प्रकार 2 उद्धरण": 제2종 ×2 are unmatched ordinals in the source, so
     the "2" must survive. Fixed the real error (उद्धरण → प्रमाणित प्रति) and kept
     "श्रेणी 2".

Reviewer rows I believe are wrong / were overridden (NOT applied)
  5. a#41 / b#43 / b#46 / b#47 — Indian लाख/crore regrouping (TWD 15,70,000 /
     15,79,589 / 2.5 करोड़ / 3 करोड़). Not applied: ACCEPTED-hi mandates international
     digits, and regrouping would desynchronise the amounts from every other locale
     and from the `numbers` gate. I agree with the supervisor here.
  6. a#21 — the reviewer asked to unify on हिन्दी. ACCEPTED-hi inverts this (हिंदी in
     prose, हिन्दी only as the autonym) and the repo test pins the FAQ question
     "क्या हिंदी में परामर्श संभव है?". Followed ACCEPTED, not the reviewer.
  7. a#10 / a#11 / b#45 — the reviewer's suggested wording inserts भारत / "भारतीय
     मार्ग नहीं" / "भारत से उल्टा". Not applied as written: the checker's
     `nationality` gate lists भारत/भारतीय as forbidden target-only terms, and R2
     forbids claims about the reader's own country. Used the neutral generalisation
     instead ("अपने देश", "ताइवान से बाहर", "ताइवान में वाहन दाईं ओर चलते हैं").
  8. a#17 / a#18 / b#10 — link rows. /ko/ links are already remapped (0 left). The
     Hangul-slug wei-wei-lawyer.com link in 005 and the Invest Taiwan `lang=jpn`
     parameter in 011 are byte-identical to the Korean source; changing either makes
     `links` report missing/extra. Skipped per ACCEPTED-hi.
  9. a#4 / a#45 — "कोरियाई बोल सकने वाली/वाले ताइवान अधिवक्ता" no longer exists in
     any Hindi column (R1 relabelling already removed it). Nothing to fix.
 10. a#9 — the quoted sentence ("भले कोरियाई मूल कंपनी ताइवान में प्रवेश करे…") is not
